### Packages

<!-- Project-specific / TypeScript-Packages -->

### Types

- Use `type` for unions and intersections; use `interface` for `extends`/`implements` contracts.
- Prefer immutability: mark never-reassigned properties `readonly`, freeze literal collections with `as const`, return new arrays/objects instead of mutating inputs.
- Prefer composition over inheritance; compose small classes, each with one responsibility.
- Prefer passing dependencies in (constructor injection) over module-level singletons.
<!-- Project-specific / TypeScript-Types -->

### Functions

- Consolidate more than two parameters into one destructured options object.
- Use `async`/`await`; do not mix callbacks and promises in the same code path.
<!-- Project-specific / TypeScript-Functions -->

### Comments

- Write doc comments in JSDoc format.
- Refer to [TypeScript JSDoc Reference](https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/jsdoc-supported.html) for supported tags.
<!-- Project-specific / TypeScript-Comments -->

### Errors

- Throw `Error` subclasses, never strings or plain objects; chain the cause: `throw new PaymentError("charge failed", { cause: error })`.
- Never leave a promise floating: await it, return it, or hand it to a handler; never write an empty `catch`.
- Cancel with `AbortController` and pass its `signal` through every call that can wait.
<!-- Project-specific / TypeScript-Errors -->

### Concurrency

- Start independent operations with `Promise.all` or `Promise.allSettled`, not one `await` at a time in a loop.
<!-- Project-specific / TypeScript-Concurrency -->
